      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a015331a6fd0876a51d5148|full_name}: If the DJ is in an instance with other people, you'd want to tweak the world so that the DJ can watch a different stream without the URL being synced. \n\nBut for now the mediamtx used to be called rtsp-simple-server, rtsp is the protocol you'll see being used by VRCDN to have very low latency streaming, like with TopazChat, I can stream to and from Japan and its 1 second of latency.\n\nFor a local stream its closer to 0.1 seconds",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
