  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-09-09T06:55:19.581Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I know this is a niche ask but it would be safe and relatively simple to add local NDI support to vrchat (considering there are ready to use unity plugins for it).\n\nWhat this would allow is VR dj's to have a local feed in their instance for realtime world response to their performance as the other people in the world see the streamed video as they perform (which enhances the experience for the performer and improves their quality of their performance).\n\nIt would also help other people who want to test world encoded data in realtime without having deal with latency and waste bandwidth on streaming services.",
